# `Where` in title case is the wrong case (DS0104), not SQL; only capitals count as SQL.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | Where amount > 1 | Select amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..53
  PIPELINE@0..52
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..36
      IDENT@20..25 "Where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..36
        NAME_REF@26..32
          IDENT@26..32 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
        GT@33..34 ">"
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        LITERAL@35..36
          LONG@35..36 "1"
    WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
    PIPE@37..38 "|"
    WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
    PROJECT_OP@39..52
      IDENT@39..45 "Select"
      WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@46..52
        NAME_REF@46..52
          IDENT@46..52 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@52..53 "\n"

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `Where`
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | Where amount > 1 | Select amount
  |                     ^^^^^ operator names are case-sensitive
  |
  = help: write `where`

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `Select`
  --> query:1:40
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | Where amount > 1 | Select amount
  |                                        ^^^^^^ not a DataScript operator
  |
  = help: to choose or compute columns, use `project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 1 | project amount
which parses without errors
